{"id":"breast-ca","cards":[{"id":"breastc649a99d","l":1,"f":"<b>Inspection</b>?","b":"skin oedema/peau d'orange, nipple position (normal vs retracted), visible masses/skin changes.","c":"Breast examination"},{"id":"breast3b60c6d9","l":1,"f":"<b>Describe any mass</b>?","b":"side + exact location/quadrant/clock position, size, mobility, fixation to skin or deep tissues, tenderness. Finish one breast, then the other.","c":"Breast examination"},{"id":"breast99575b83","l":1,"f":"<b>Axilla</b>?","b":"right axilla with the left hand and vice versa, arm supported. Nodes: number, size, discrete vs matted, mobile vs fixed.","c":"Breast examination"},{"id":"breaste4d1e3a0","l":1,"f":"<b>Metastatic examination</b>?","b":"abdomen (ascites, organomegaly) and back/skeleton (bone metastases).","c":"Breast examination"},{"id":"breaste91b377c","l":2,"f":"Most common presentation of breast cancer in Saudi Arabia","b":"<b>painless breast mass</b>","c":"Breast examination"},{"id":"breast3ea1c3d6","l":2,"f":"Palpable 3-cm mass after history &amp; exam → <b>imaging, then biopsy</b> ; mammogram is ordered to look for <b>microcalcifications</b> ; young woman with bloody discharge","b":"<b>ultrasound</b>","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"breastea27ee53","l":2,"f":"70-year-old <b>man</b> with an ulcerating breast mass and axillary nodes","b":"initial step <b>mammogram</b> (then biopsy) — not excision or antibiotics","c":"Investigations"},{"id":"breast40554e5a","l":1,"f":"<b>Incomplete</b> — Action?","b":"Additional imaging","c":"Investigations › BI-RADS"},{"id":"breast51dcebd8","l":1,"f":"<b>Negative</b> — Action?","b":"Routine follow-up","c":"Investigations › BI-RADS"},{"id":"breast9015d731","l":1,"f":"<b>Benign</b> — Action?","b":"Routine follow-up","c":"Investigations › BI-RADS"},{"id":"breaste9339746","l":1,"f":"<b>Probably benign (&lt; 2% malignancy)</b> — Action?","b":"<b>Short-interval follow-up (3–6 months)</b>","c":"Investigations › BI-RADS"},{"id":"breastd35ed15d","l":1,"f":"<b>Suspicious</b> — Action?","b":"<b>Biopsy</b>","c":"Investigations › BI-RADS"},{"id":"breast8a9e5fa1","l":1,"f":"<b>Highly suspicious</b> — Action?","b":"<b>Biopsy</b>","c":"Investigations › BI-RADS"},{"id":"breast670db13b","l":1,"f":"<b>Core needle biopsy</b>?","b":"palpable → clinical core under local; non-palpable → <b>US-guided</b>, <b>stereotactic (mammography-guided)</b>, or <b>MRI-guided</b> (most difficult).","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breastb6101a8c","l":1,"f":"<b>Never excise an undiagnosed mass first</b>?","b":"if malignant, the oncological margins won't have been taken and surgery must be repeated.","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breast10a8a717","l":2,"f":"Best initial diagnostic step for a breast mass","b":"<b>core biopsy</b> (not FNA or surgery)","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breastdf636379","l":1,"f":"<b>1. Diagnosis</b> — Details?","b":"Benign vs malignant","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breastcc41e670","l":1,"f":"<b>2. Histological type</b> — Details?","b":"<b>Ductal (most common)</b>, lobular (2nd); mucinous, papillary, medullary","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breastf104096f","l":1,"f":"<b>3. Grade</b> — Details?","b":"1 well · 2 intermediate · 3 poorly differentiated — <b>grade ≠ stage</b>","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breast7b1b9a99","l":1,"f":"<b>4. ER, PR</b> — Details?","b":"Benefit from hormonal therapy","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breast008d9bfd","l":1,"f":"<b>5. HER2</b> — Details?","b":"~15%, aggressive; HER2-targeted therapy","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breast246ceb89","l":1,"f":"<b>6. Ki-67</b> — Details?","b":"Proliferation: 5% slow vs 90% aggressive","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breast45121c80","l":2,"f":"Most common type of breast cancer","b":"<b>invasive ductal carcinoma</b> (\"intraductal\" in the recall)","c":"Investigations › Biopsy"},{"id":"breast1479f65f","l":1,"f":"<b>Luminal A</b> — Grade / Ki-67?","b":"Grade 1, Ki-67 low (≤ 10%)","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breast38b5b672","l":1,"f":"<b>Luminal A</b> — Behaviour &amp; systemic treatment?","b":"Best prognosis → <b>hormonal therapy alone</b>","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breast0612fc9b","l":1,"f":"<b>Luminal B</b> — ER/PR?","b":"ER+, usually PR+","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breastf7cb326a","l":1,"f":"<b>Luminal B</b> — Grade / Ki-67?","b":"Grade 2–3, Ki-67 higher","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breast9cde7fce","l":1,"f":"<b>Luminal B</b> — Behaviour &amp; systemic treatment?","b":"More aggressive → <b>chemo + hormonal</b>","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breastd5aa7574","l":1,"f":"<b>HER2-positive</b> — ER/PR?","b":"Variable","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breastf9106643","l":1,"f":"<b>HER2-positive</b> — Behaviour &amp; systemic treatment?","b":"Aggressive → <b>chemo + anti-HER2 (trastuzumab)</b> ± endocrine","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breast013ab57d","l":1,"f":"<b>Triple-negative</b> — Behaviour &amp; systemic treatment?","b":"Very aggressive (young) → <b>chemotherapy only</b>","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breastb725b420","l":2,"f":"ER−, PR−, <b>HER2+</b>","b":"<b>trastuzumab (Herceptin)</b> (tamoxifen, letrozole and goserelin need ER+)","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breast99209b24","l":2,"f":"95-year-old, devastating comorbidities, ulcerating T3N0M0 <b>luminal A</b> (ER/PR ~100%, Ki-67 5%, grade 1)","b":"<b>hormonal therapy only</b>","c":"Biological subtypes"},{"id":"breast63133512","l":1,"f":"<b>I–II</b> — Meaning?","b":"Early: small/localized ± limited nodes","c":"Staging & the metastatic screen"},{"id":"breastde71bd7a","l":1,"f":"<b>Stage III</b> — Meaning?","b":"Locally advanced, confined to breast + regional nodes","c":"Staging & the metastatic screen"},{"id":"breast4b985799","l":1,"f":"<b>Stage IV</b> — Meaning?","b":"Metastatic — 5-year survival &lt; 18%; ~95% non-surgical (chemo, hormonal, targeted)","c":"Staging & the metastatic screen"},{"id":"breast58fef4cd","l":2,"f":"Breast cancer 5 years ago, now 3 weeks of <b>neck pain</b> without trauma","b":"<b>spinal MRI</b> (bone metastasis/cord compression)","c":"Staging & the metastatic screen"},{"id":"breast5f0ccac3","l":2,"f":"Metastatic (brain + bone) triple-negative cancer","b":"keyed <b>palliative care</b> (the doctor: stage IV is treated systemically — palliative chemotherapy; no breast surgery)","c":"Staging & the metastatic screen"},{"id":"breast1d2b13c8","l":2,"f":"Single most important prognostic factor","b":"<b>number of involved axillary nodes</b>","c":"Staging & the metastatic screen"},{"id":"breast3d0377e4","l":2,"f":"\"Cellulitis\" recurring 5 times despite antibiotics","b":"<b>skin biopsy</b>","c":"Inflammatory breast cancer"},{"id":"breast32510d39","l":2,"f":"Triple-negative with <b>one positive axillary node</b>","b":"<b>neoadjuvant chemotherapy, then surgery</b>","c":"Treatment › Systemic therapy"},{"id":"breast9a9f77b4","l":2,"f":"Locally advanced (stage III, skin involvement, 3 nodes) invasive ductal carcinoma","b":"<b>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</b> first","c":"Treatment › Systemic therapy"},{"id":"breast5f409167","l":1,"f":"<b>Multicentric / multifocal disease</b> — Why?","b":"Can't remove adequately while conserving","c":"Treatment › Locoregional therapy"},{"id":"breast73736557","l":1,"f":"<b>Large tumor in a small breast</b> — Why?","b":"Neoadjuvant chemo may shrink it","c":"Treatment › Locoregional therapy"},{"id":"breast0aee559f","l":1,"f":"<b>BRCA1/2</b> — Why?","b":"Relative contraindication","c":"Treatment › Locoregional therapy"},{"id":"breastf0a0a949","l":1,"f":"<b>Pregnancy</b> — Why?","b":"No RT during pregnancy","c":"Treatment › Locoregional therapy"},{"id":"breast6e358a83","l":1,"f":"<b>Previous chest/breast radiation</b> — Why?","b":"Repeat RT unsafe (toxicity, secondary sarcoma)","c":"Treatment › Locoregional therapy"},{"id":"breast7f5759c9","l":1,"f":"<b>Collagen vascular disease (lupus)</b> — Why?","b":"Flares with RT","c":"Treatment › Locoregional therapy"},{"id":"breast4b02f188","l":2,"f":"ER+ cancer in a 65-year-old with <b>previous bilateral breast radiation for Hodgkin's</b>","b":"<b>simple mastectomy</b> (can't re-irradiate)","c":"Treatment › Locoregional therapy"},{"id":"breast0379e1c9","l":2,"f":"Breast mass with clinically and radiologically <b>benign-looking nodes</b>","b":"<b>breast-conserving surgery + sentinel node biopsy</b>","c":"Treatment › Locoregional therapy"},{"id":"breastab18fd41","l":2,"f":"Retroareolar ER/PR+ HER2− mass with nipple retraction, node-negative (recall without choices)","b":"<b>central lumpectomy removing the nipple–areola complex + SLNB + radiotherapy</b> (or mastectomy + SLNB), then endocrine therapy","c":"Treatment › Locoregional therapy"},{"id":"breastf162a9ce","l":2,"f":"DCIS (calcifications)","b":"<b>lumpectomy + radiotherapy</b>","c":"Treatment › DCIS"},{"id":"breast6b21bd1b","l":2,"f":"<b>Paget disease</b> of the nipple = a <b>superficial manifestation of an underlying breast cancer</b> (eczema-like nipple change","b":"biopsy)","c":"Treatment › DCIS"},{"id":"breast7733d43a","l":1,"f":"<b>ALND</b>?","b":"removes ~20–30 nodes; needed for <b>gross nodal disease</b>; lymphedema up to <b>~40%</b>, shoulder dysfunction.","c":"Treatment › Axillary surgery"},{"id":"breastd0fed4fe","l":1,"f":"<b>SLNB</b>?","b":"first draining node(s), usually ~3 nodes; radioactive tracer + blue dye → gamma probe; ± frozen section. Lymphedema <b>~3–4%</b>. A blue/hot node is the sentinel, <b>not necessarily malignant</b>.","c":"Treatment › Axillary surgery"},{"id":"breastd5e8cc05","l":2,"f":"Purpose of sentinel node biopsy","b":"<b>assess the extent of lymphatic involvement</b> (staging the axilla)","c":"Treatment › Axillary surgery"},{"id":"breast7a1ddbec","l":1,"f":"<b>Interval cancer</b>?","b":"diagnosed between two screening mammograms (~10–15%) — not automatically an error.","c":"Other points"},{"id":"breast9cbb13b9","l":1,"f":"<b>Genetic (BRCA) testing</b>?","b":"targeted: age &lt; 50, triple-negative, <b>male breast cancer</b>, breast + ovarian family pattern.","c":"Other points"},{"id":"breastdd088625","l":1,"f":"<b>Screening</b>?","b":"goal = detect cancer before it is palpable (DCIS/microcalcifications). Average risk ~40–50 to ~75 (national program); high risk earlier (~30).","c":"Other points"},{"id":"breast697cf93d","l":1,"f":"<b>Breast MRI</b>?","b":"young patients, implants, before/after neoadjuvant chemo, BRCA/high risk, when mammogram/US are insufficient.","c":"Other points"}]}